course: dictionary
lesson: 856
title: Beyond: far, late, too much, unknown
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Beyond is a small word with big jobs. It can tell you where something is, when something happens, how much there is, or what is unknown. The words around it are its context, and they show which job it is doing.
explain: «The lovely canary-coloured cart lies on its side, smashed beyond repair.» Beyond repair means too damaged to fix. The cart cannot be mended, so beyond means past what is possible. Ask: does "too much for" fit here? If it does, you have found the meaning.
explain: «Headlines are written to make you click and can be misleading, so read beyond the headline.» Here beyond means further than the headline, so you read the rest of the story. The word headline tells you beyond is on the far side of it.
explain: In «out there, beyond — beyond!» the word points to something far away that nobody can see yet. Beyond can also mean the unknown, or what some people believe comes after death. Check each meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you are right.
fact: Beyond can mean on the far side of something, further away than it.
fact: Beyond can mean later than a certain time, or more than a certain amount, as in counting beyond 100.
fact: Beyond can mean too much for something, as in «beyond belief» or «beyond repair».
fact: The beyond is the unknown, or what some people believe comes after death.
fact: «To infinity and beyond» is a famous phrase meaning on and on with no end.
exercise: «The town lies beyond the mountains.» What does beyond mean here? | Inside a cave | Covered in snow | *On the far side of the mountains | Before the mountains, close to your feet
exercise: «The cart was smashed beyond repair.» What does beyond repair mean? | Repaired twice already | Very fast on the road | *Too damaged to fix | Newly painted and shiny
exercise: Ayaan counts and says, «I can count beyond 100!» What does beyond mean here? | Hidden under 100 | *Greater than 100 | Exactly 100 | Less than 100
test: «The view from the top was beyond belief.» What does beyond belief mean? | *Too amazing to believe | Very cold, like ice | Easy to see from far away
test: Mei says Buddhists believe nirvana is «a peace beyond suffering». What does this suggest? | Being very hungry | Loud music at a party | *Peace that goes past suffering, where suffering is left behind
exam: «Headlines can be misleading, so read beyond the headline.» What does beyond mean here? | *Past the headline, into the rest of the story | Only the first word of the headline | Read the rest of the story, past the headline | Read it upside down
